WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.038
GPGME 2.3.1 fixes

00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:03.899
a critical double

00:00:03.711 --> 00:00:04.618
free reachable

00:00:05.142 --> 00:00:07.111
GnuPG released GPGME

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.844
2.3.1 after a

00:00:08.656 --> 00:00:10.542
crafted OpenPGP key

00:00:10.614 --> 00:00:11.380
with a very

00:00:11.192 --> 00:00:12.264
long user ID

00:00:12.276 --> 00:00:12.983
was found to

00:00:12.795 --> 00:00:13.691
trigger a double

00:00:13.503 --> 00:00:14.422
free that can

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:15.248
leak data from

00:00:15.071 --> 00:00:16.108
applications

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:17.538
The flaw was

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:18.375
found by Johan

00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:19.648
Carlsson and reported

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.721
via GitLab on

00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:21.582
Nov 12

00:00:21.807 --> 00:00:23.080
disclosure was moved

00:00:22.892 --> 00:00:24.589
up from Nov 25

00:00:24.484 --> 00:00:25.155
because of the

00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:26.370
Ruby2Shell bug

00:00:26.894 --> 00:00:28.026
Initially we set

00:00:27.837 --> 00:00:30.632
2026-11-25 for a

00:00:30.444 --> 00:00:31.823
coordinated disclosure

00:00:32.047 --> 00:00:32.566
due to the

00:00:32.377 --> 00:00:33.969
new Ruby2Shell bug

00:00:33.781 --> 00:00:34.853
GitLab had to

00:00:34.665 --> 00:00:36.162
update earlier and

00:00:36.057 --> 00:00:36.893
thus we also

00:00:36.705 --> 00:00:37.648
disclosed

00:00:38.166 --> 00:00:39.180
Full story on

00:00:38.991 --> 00:00:39.887
the dashboard
